sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, container runtime (ADR 0250, docs/reference/development-containers.md#processes): the status of a Process in an Instance container. No command starts it; a Process list does.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · Process lists
  %% kind: process.inspect
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>reached over ssh
  Note over GW: A list needs a state<br/>last inspection is over 30 s old
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - neither Prometheus nor the Node agent sees a container's units, so the list keeps the last completed inspection's state, observed_at and reason, and starts a read off the request; only a never-inspected Process has no observation
  %%> - at most four reads start per list, oldest observed_at first and never-inspected first; one read per Process at a time
  %%> - each Process waits 30 s after its durable last outcome, including after cache eviction
  %%> - a running or unfinished Instance migration answers unknown with instance.lifecycle_busy and starts no read
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-process-container
  SW->>N: Read the unit<br/>Ansible · tags process
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - `systemctl is-active` in the container through `incus exec`
  SW->>SW: Keep the result<br/>process-command-assets
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - publishes the unit's state; journal lines of a log read go only to the vault
  alt the read passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    Note over GW: Keep the state and time<br/>refresh after 30 s
  else the read fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    Note over GW: Replace state with unknown<br/>keep failure reason and time
  end
